  "reasoning": "A checkpoint can avoid at most the calculation a restart repeats. The largest admissible program calculates in about 3 ms, and the largest archived in-service calculation took 15.5 ms, against restart-to-terminal latencies of 0.71 to 1.99 s that a checkpoint restore would also pay. Even a zero-cost checkpoint fails the gate, so checkpoint encode, store and restore costs were not measured.",
